  "notes": [
    "Compiler and output executables are arm64. The Python 3.7 driver itself reports x86_64 under Rosetta; subprocess compilers and CMake run as arm64.",
    "C uses CMake/Ninja with four jobs. Odin and Zig use the checked-in Python wrappers, which configure and invoke CMake/Make for shared C dependencies.",
    "Each fresh_seconds result is a single build in a new source/build copy. Zig global and local caches start empty. OS filesystem and Apple SDK caches are not flushed.",
    "Each edit changes PLAYER_SHOT_SPEED to a previously unbuilt value: 621, 622, then 623. Source changes occur only in ignored scratch copies.",
    "Zig clean_warm_tools_seconds is a separate single build after cleaning native libraries and moving aside its local cache; its populated global tool cache is retained.",
    "No tests, downloads, asset generation, app launch or store packaging are timed. Source-copy setup is outside the timed interval.",
    "Command paths below use <repo> as a placeholder for the local checkout."
